  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The series of positive multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> is divided into sets : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the sum of the elements in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>11</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;set is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6993",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></math></p><p>Now, the number of elements in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>11</mn><mtext>th&#160;</mtext></msup></math>&nbsp;set will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>The total number of elements up to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup></math>&nbsp;set will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>11</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup></math>&nbsp;set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>101</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>102</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>121</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Sum&nbsp;of these elements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>101</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>102</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>121</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>101</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>121</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6993</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
